{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1504703359,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyNzQ3Nzg1NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1798#issuecomment-327477854"},"message":"Valid concern!  Ideally v6 should operate similar to v5, and thus before anything, would be worth may be coming back to still open in annex http://git-annex.branchable.com/bugs/Too_difficult_if_not_impossible_to_explicitly_add__47__keep_file_under_git___40__not_annex__41___in_v6_without_employing_.gitattributes/","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1505391560,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyOTQ2NDU1Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1798#issuecomment-329464553"},"message":"Well, I did kind of come back to it, but it's really about a side-effect, not a fundamental thing. In general, Joey clearly stated, that `.gitattributes` is the way to go. Using a per-call `-c annex.largefiles=whatever` will not work, since it is insufficient to do this only when adding a file the first time. We would need to keep track of all files, that were explicitly added to git and call basically any annex command involving those files with that option again. So, we would end up building our own `.gitattributes` while still not being able to do it properly, since we don't always know what files will be touched by the smudge filtering.\nUntil now, we have the option to decide between git and annex on a per file basis.\n\nSo, from my point of view there are two options:\n 1. a) keep that option and write files, that were explicitly added to git into `.gitattributes`. In the long run and depending on use cases, this might become a nightmare of a `.gitattributes` file. If we want to do that, how do we approach analyzing `.gitattributes` for matching, contradicting or identical entries?\n\n    b) as above, but don't care about the possibly messed up `.gitattributes` and leave it to the user. Basically we are saying: That option is a convenience to add an entry to `.gitattributes`, but there's nothing more: we do not maintain that file for you.\n\n 3. or we simply don't allow to add anything directly to git via a datalad command's option, but only via user-editing of `.gitattributes` (and special cases we manage on our own without user interaction)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1505392221,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyOTQ2Njg3NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1798#issuecomment-329466875"},"message":"2 wouldn't work since there is still just git add people could use\n\nI think the issue shopping be fixed at annex level, since that is what knows if any particular path was under git or annex... I do appreciate possible tech difficulty of implementation, but anything else wouldn't be robust IMHO. What is your thoughts ATM @joeyh?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1505392513,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyOTQ2ODAwMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1798#issuecomment-329468001"},"message":"\u003e 2 wouldn't work since there is still just git add people could use\n\nThat doesn't matter in v6. ;-)\n\nWe can not revert `git add` to work in v6 like it was a plain git or v5 repo. If people expect this, they are simply wrong about a fundamental thing.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1505392837,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyOTQ2OTIwOQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1798#issuecomment-329469209"},"message":"To be clear: \"since there is still just git add people could use\" doesn't make sense to me as an argument. This is true in any case. And I don't know how that matters. `git add` will respect `.gitattributes`","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1505393061,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyOTQ3MDEzNQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1798#issuecomment-329470135"},"message":"RRight! Forgot about that. I think we should at least issue a big day warning when adding --to-git is used in v6. I would still not prevent it entirely.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"819663238374c863923453c36b916c251f565216"},"timestamp":1505395180,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyOTQ3OTIzMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1798#issuecomment-329479231"},"message":"So, this is basically a vote in favor of 1b)?\n\nAm 14.09.2017 14:44 schrieb \"Yaroslav Halchenko\" \u003cnotifications@github.com\u003e:\n\n\u003e RRight! Forgot about that. I think we should at least issue a big day\n\u003e warning when adding --to-git is used in v6. I would still not prevent it\n\u003e entirely.\n\u003e\n\u003e —\n\u003e You are receiving this because you authored the thread.\n\u003e Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\n\u003e \u003chttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1798#issuecomment-329470135\u003e,\n\u003e or mute the thread\n\u003e \u003chttps://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/AKAw_dsjCvLeAENkAPmuoNx1iE0FPso2ks5siR-lgaJpZM4POLQY\u003e\n\u003e .\n\u003e","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1505395822,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDMyOTQ4MjE4NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1798#issuecomment-329482184"},"message":"I guess so ;-)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1538505646,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQyNjM4NTcyMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/1798#issuecomment-426385721"},"message":"This issue is now